{"id":"6edd93f8-7f8f-45dd-9f51-ae4dbe9f3667","object":"chat.completion","created":1785035487,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mutual = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mutual, u, v))\\n\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n\\n    parent = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        parent[n] = n\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rx < ry:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns {\"mst_edges\": [...], \"total_weight\": number}. Case has \"nodes\", \"core_distance\", \"distances\". Compute mutual reachability for each pair (undirected, sort endpoints). Then run Kruskal with union-find to get MST edges and total weight. Important: edge tie-breaking: sort by mutual reachability weight first, then by endpoint IDs (lexicographically? probably string compare). Ensure deterministic.\n\nWe'll output Python code.\n\nConstraints: No external libraries, no randomness.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Parse nodes list, core distance dict, distance list.\n2. Create list of edges: for each [u,v,d] in distances, compute mutual_reach = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d). Endpoints canonical order: sorted (u,v) since strings. Store as (u,v,mutual_reach).\n3. Sort edges: primary key mutual_reach, secondary key u, tertiary key v (or just tuple (mutual_reach, u, v)).\n4. Union-Find class with parent dict, find with path compression.\n5. Iterate sorted edges, if find(u) != find(v), union, add edge to mst_edges, add weight to total.\n6. After loop, if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes)-1: raise ValueError (disconnected).\n7. Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}.\n\nNote: mst_edges list entries must be [u, v, weight] where u and v strings, weight number. Should we keep as list of lists? Yes, per schema: prefixItems [string, string, number]. Return as Python list of lists.\n\nEdge case: distances may contain both directions? Usually undirected, but specification says \"distances\" list, each entry [node1, node2, distance]. We treat each as one undirected edge. Ensure we don't double count. Input seems to have each pair once.\n\nAlso ensure no mutation of case.\n\nNow write code accordingly.\n\nOutput format: {\"implementation\": \"...\"} where \"...\" is Python source as JSON string.\n\nWe'll produce the JSON object."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2021,"completion_tokens":846,"total_tokens":2867,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":460},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":101},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}